  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Al Murunah +: Supporting Al-Murunah project integrating NBS with household resilience, focus on gender norms</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Al-Murunah+ enhances the core Al-Murunah project by integrating NBS with household resilience-building to promote positive gender norms across Al-Murunah pilot sites in Egypt, Jordan, Lebanon, and the Occupied Palestinian Territories (OPTs). By supporting sustainable agriculture and water management with targeted household-level interventions&#x2014;including asset transfers and Islamic revolving funds&#x2014;the project empowers vulnerable groups, particularly women. It positions gender equity not only as a social imperative but also as a critical enabler for climate adaptation, water security, and sustainable livelihoods. This holistic model amplifies environmental outcomes while driving economic and social development.</narrative>
  </description>
